The v5 slide face serves two incompatible consumer contracts for its
authenticated rebase entries, and neither the r87 all-signed gate nor the
r92 mapping-writability split satisfies both.  r92's real-machine window
settled it: the sheng-v5 probe printed wr=1 for all eight entries because
slide_mapping is only ever handed sms_max_prot (vm_shared_region.c
sr_file_mappings pass), so the writability split degenerated to
plain-everywhere and dyld's AUTDA at the r85 wall-85 slot (unslid
.25.dylddata 0x1E8D37228, diversity 0x9abf, consumer dyld+0xb38b74 this
boot) failed on the plain store 165us after the probe row -- the same
slot that r87-r91 proved passes AUTDA when stored full-width.  s84's own
sc25 page-209 chain also shows both families interleaved inside one
writable mapping (0x6ae1 self-ref next to 0xb5ab), so no mapping-level
signal can ever separate them.

Split on the entry instead: target == slot marks the self-referential
anchor family (the ObjC root-metaclass isa self-pointers; libobjc reads
them raw and ISA_MASK-masks them, the r89-r91 wall-86 far = [tag][VA]
with the VA part bit-exact across three generations), so they must stay
plain.  Every other authenticated entry is consumed through AUTDA (the
wall-85 family) and keeps the full hardware pacda form, which r87-r91
proved passes.  Plain rebases (auth bit clear) are untouched.  The
si_writable field stays only as probe telemetry; the sheng-v5 probe is
widened to 32 rows and now prints the self-reference verdict and the
clean target alongside the stored form.

